     dimension-mismatch errors. Startup now detects the drift, wipes and
     re-embeds the KB automatically (PostgreSQL column is recreated).
+
+## Hotfix: embedding-dimension reconciliation (MVP patch 3)
+
+28. **Boot-time dimension probe** (`reconcile_embedding_dimension`): a fresh
+    install with `EMBEDDING_DIM=1024` crashed because the OpenRouter model
+    (`nvidia/nemotron-3-embed-1b:free`) actually returns 2048-dim vectors —
+    pgvector rejected every insert ("expected 1024 dimensions, not 2048") and
+    the backend exited before serving a single request. The stored-row drift
+    heal can't see this on an empty database, so startup now asks the live
+    embedding API for ONE probe vector, trusts that width, recreates the
+    pgvector column at the real dimension, adopts the dimension in-process
+    and re-ingests. A loud log line tells the operator to fix EMBEDDING_DIM
+    in .env to make it permanent. `.env.example` default corrected to 2048.
+29. **KB ingestion is non-fatal at boot**: if the embedding API is down or
+    over quota, the backend now boots with an empty knowledge base and a
+    logged error instead of exiting (chat/agent keep working; guidance
+    answers just lack citations). `/api/health` now also reports the
+    effective `embedding_dim` for quick diagnosis.
